- **Labour Force Survey (LFS):** Yes, it is mandatory. Statistics Canada's survey record says participation is mandatory for adults under the authority of the Statistics Act.
- **Canadian Income Survey (CIS):** No, it is voluntary. The record says responding to the survey is voluntary. The CIS is given to a sub-sample of LFS respondents, but it is voluntary even for them. Income data are also taken from Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) tax files.

Source: Statistics Canada Integrated Metadata Database, LFS (survey 3701) and CIS (survey 5200). The LFS reference period is usually the week containing the 15th of the month. The CIS record shown covers the 2025 reference year, collected 2026-01-18 to 2026-07-07.

